Here is your first example:

> HS.model <- ' visual  =~ x1 + x2 + x3

+               textual =~ x4 + x5 + x6
+               speed   =~ x7 + x8 + x9
+
+               y ~ visual + textual + speed
+ '

>
> Data <- HolzingerSwineford1939
> Data$y <- c(rep(1,200), rep(0,101))
>
> fit <- sem(HS.model, data = Data, ordered = "y", std.lv <http://std.lv> = TRUE)

Error in muthen1984(Data = X[[g]], ov.names = ov.names[[g]], ov.types = ov.types,  :

  lavaan ERROR: some categories of variable `y' are empty in group 1; frequencies are [200 0]

Your second and third examples use:

> HS.model <- ' visual  =~ x1 + x2 + x3

+               textual =~ x4 + x5 + x6
+               speed   =~ x7 + x8 + x9
+
+               # factor variances + covariances
+               visual ~~ 1*visual
+               textual ~~ 1*textual
+               speed ~~ 1*speed
+               visual ~~ textual + speed
+               textual ~~ speed
+
+               # residual variances indicators
+               x1 ~~ x1; x2 ~~ x2; x3 ~~ x3
+               x4 ~~ x4; x5 ~~ x5; x6 ~~ x6
+               x7 ~~ x7; x8 ~~ x8; x9 ~~ x9
+
+               y ~ visual + textual + speed
+ '
>
The following statement fails as you said:
> fit <- lavaan(HS.model, data = Data, ordered = "y")

Error in muthen1984(Data = X[[g]], ov.names = ov.names[[g]], ov.types = ov.types,  :

  lavaan ERROR: some categories of variable `y' are empty in group 1; frequencies are [200 0]

However, the third possibility fails also:

> fit <- lavaan(HS.model, data = Data, ordered = "y", auto.th <http://auto.th> = TRUE, int.ov.free = TRUE)

Error in muthen1984(Data = X[[g]], ov.names = ov.names[[g]], ov.types = ov.types,  :

  lavaan ERROR: some categories of variable `y' are empty in group 1; frequencies are [200 0]

